Executive Summary

There has been significant reduction of headcount from the implementation of AI within some of the largest organisations in the world with reductions of 14,000 of 350,000 Amazon corporate workers as a part of wave of cuts (Callum Jones, 2025). Other companies such as Microsoft, Meta, Instagram and Facebook and Alphabet have all laid of tens of thousands of workers in the past three months (Callum Jones, 2025). Approximately 15% of HR roles are to be targeted within Amazon. Currently small companies require additional staff for support services. Which creates an expensive cost with training and reoccurring requirements. The belief is that these efficient can be scaled to smaller companies.

The target customers for the products are SME’s who cannot justify call centres and dedicated support teams as a part of their service offerings. Larger corporations have stricter SLA’s and terms thus immediate business with them difficult to engage with. Freon Chat is a highly personal and rapid moving organisations that is ready to leverage the early market advantage.

The expectation is the requirement of £30,000 of investment with 10-25% of shares to be allocated for additional members of staff.

Background
Currently a serious push within the market for implementation of chatbot services is occurring. This has started dating back from the 1970s from the formation of ‘Dialogue Systems’, continued to approximately 20 years of continued development until the first ‘chatbots’ emerged (Lee J.H et al 2020). Now there is the release to the public of OpenAi’s LLM ChatGPT which occurred in June 2020 which provides the basis for the next push in chatbot functionalities.

The continued development has led to exponentially increasing complexity for Chatbots showcased by the several folds increase from GPT-1 to GPT-3: 117 million to 175 billion (OpenAI 2019). These models understand greater context, nuance and even humour (Bernard Marr, 2023).

The Business Idea

There is an increasing availability of tools that make chatbots an effective resource for the displacement of call centres and for small business to provide support services. The lack of support available is often due to the fact small companies tend to have small head counts thus do not have the required manpower to facilitate 24/7 customer support coverage.
The increasing market for LLMs is the basis for the consultancy services. There is the expectation of many competing consultancies, freelancers and offshore developers offering services within the web development space– this project aims to differentiate with chatbot implementation with strong UX development experience as the core product offering. Customers may also be consulted for peripheral services related to web application development with tailored and off-the-shelf solutions as a part of the product offerings. 
Small business is the target for this proposition to leverage a lower entry barrier, and smaller start-up cost requirement. Business solutions can be delivered with little initial investment. 
To ensure market ownership, the following are the benefits of the consultancy: 
-	Flexible pricing point
-	Niche Market segmentation
-	Personal & Face-to-face consultancy
The basics: such as a website (host & DNS) with basic automation for ensuring customers can get in contact are solid solutions and would provide the means to display the product portfolio

New Venture Formation

The Business name of ‘Freon Chat’ which is part from the coastal areas of the Netherlands. With Freon meaning friend.

The Domain name of www.freonchat.com is available at a very low cost on GoDaddy with a price point of $12.19USD for the first year (Appendix 1)

The company name is not registered at the Companies House website. There is Freon Ltd which is which appears to be a holding company. The companies are similar in name but in completely different industry segments to not dis-allow ‘Freon Chat’ which serves a distinct purpose. The distinction is well conveyed in ‘Freon Chat’s’ name.
Other similar company names are:
-	Frens Limited
-	Venn Limited
-	Friends Limited

The company is initially intended to be 95-100% held by the company owner, unless significant investment and domain expertise can be provided to justify the sales of a portion of the company (20%). The almost full control of the company is to be retained to ensure that the niche skillset required for the company full functioning remains at the forefront of executive decision making. This may change in the advent of the availability of significant talent which could accelerate the company’s growth – the decision for a minority stake is to be decided at month three.
 
The small 5% is to be divided amongst the board members for work done in largely an advisory capacity to incentive well informed decision making. Due to this the company will be set up as a Limited Company guaranteed by Shares.

Initially there are no expected development hires for the company until there are multiple customer streams to ensure that there is a constant influx of work from the customer such as bug fixes and new customer features. In the case of downtime developers can begin enhancements and the development of features such as implementation of basket and checkout solutions within the Chatbot itself.

The expectation is that it would take approximately two months for there to be two clients (see timeline below). From henceforth the target after two months would be to hire one additional developer to work alongside the owner (Myself: with development and minor sales experience). This would provide adequate coverage for sales and IT related tasks until further expansion and greater work volume from clients.

The requirement of a sales agent will become apparent as a greater volume of development work is required from existing clients. The expectation is that there will be five clients by six months after which the work volume will impede the ability to managing existing and gain new clients.

The company’s initial location will be kept at a home premises (in Watford) due to the nature of the work not requiring an office and the cost saving benefits. This should make the role advertisement more competitive in the market due to WFH capabilities which should offset a portion of salary requirements.

