Market Position
                    (Figure 11.) 
    
Much of competition is employing generative AI akin to the prototype for the chatbot which uses ChatGPT as one of the many models. Others are using their own proprietary models for the purposes of the AI agent. 

The Bot Forge has showcased some good initial momentum but has not been able to build on its engagement with BNP Paribas yet and move into the corporate space. The company offers a similar product range to our intended with integration with popular applications such as Alexa, Facebook Messenger, Google Home, Slack and Microsoft Teams. Their site does not contain a pricing list.

Converse360: Does better in conveying the applications of its solutions with a range of different work cases provided such as email automation, Contact centre connectors, self-service FAQs amongst the many. Highlighting a great deal of business awareness. Charges a £500 initial start-up cost with a base support package of £145 per month up to £495 for an extended service package. With a website crawler being a part of a more expensive package at £295 – Which is felt to be a key feature and to be included in cheaper offerings of Freon Chat.

Converse360 has negative net assets (-£385,000) and a deferred income of (£148,000). Which displays a negative equity position. The company is still trading which indicates that the owners have been willing to continue with the company and expectation of future subscription income. (Converse360, 2024)

Other major technologies being used are ASR (Automatic voice recognition) which provides a major functionality for the largest of the listed competitors PolyAI which has successfully used the solution to achieve the following metrics for their clients:

•	Melting Pot generated $250k from afterhours bookings.
•	76% conversion rate for bookings at Cote Brasserie with 72% reduction to calls for employees. With 12% of calls being missed at the front of house due to front -of-house staff workloads.
•	Maintaining a 96% CSAT (customer satisfaction rating) at a banking institution.
•	A gain of 30% calls answered for a pub franchise for booking purposes resolving the need for a calls centre. With 3% revenue uplift across 140 sites.
(PolyAI, 2025)
These metrics showcase the power of their solution in providing their customers with significant added value. Showcasing the potential upsides of the implementation of generative AI and ASR.

PolyAI have shown a great deal of success with over $120M USD raised in its series A, B,C funding rounds from Khosla Ventures, Point72 Ventures and Amadeus Capital Partners. (TechCrunch 2024, Khosla Venture 2021, Amadeus Partners 2019). They have shown a great deal of success since spinning off from Cambridge.

Free solutions such as Noupe are becoming more common place in recent years with the advent of freemium software offerings. Noupe offers a comprehensive tool that integrates into nearly any site seamlessly with little UI refinement nor development required – it is an overlay.

The tool itself provides a great means for basic searches and site trawling related solutions. The price plan is for 100 (starter), 1000 (bronze),10,000 (gold) Monthly Conversations priced at FREE, $34USD and $99USD per month. 

The short comings with the solution are the limited conversation count for the free offering. The other offerings are not suitable for many of the largest enterprises – This means that there is a hard cap with the number of conversations the AI can use leaving the site open for usage abuse and customer potentially left with no AI support.

Other issues are that the chatbot does not integrate with any CRM systems or other information systems beyond documents provided and the site itself. The product works off Noupes own server architecture meaning there is little to no ownership of the solution. (Noupe)

The competition displays a young market set for much growth and opportunity. This is further showcased with Nvidea’s $5tn market evaluation largely based on the AI boom. The first company in the world to do so (Danielle Kay, 2025)

Product Marketing

Initial steps are to develop prototype chatbot for use of piloting and demos for clients to build awareness and credibility.

The initial target for business is local institutions due to the ability to engage personally, and to take advantage of local connections close to the founder.

Once there are customers established; after the creation of a portfolio the drive to push the product via web-traffic will be accelerated. The market position is to provide a technical and customer support-oriented solution. Marketing is to occur on technology related social media. Sites such as Reddit are the priority. Other means such as search Engine optimisation to ensure the product reaches the right audience.





