Work schedule
The schedule for development is based on traditional SCRUM Agile with some tailoring to ensure that there is additional time provided for the sales team to be able to input on their objectives and interface with the developer. A rigid structure has been chosen to ensure that there is regular team time, and that work progress remains easy to track. See figure 8.

Agile/SCRUM also ensures uniformity with many current business practises ensuring new hires can more seamlessly integrate into the organisation with little adjustment period.

There are expected to be some difficulty in assigning story points for features, sub-epics and epics due to a lack of knowledge surrounding all the development processes. This is expected to begin resolving itself after a few months when work is completed which would provide a basis for future work estimation visualised via burn down chart.

Board meetings are to occur on a bi-monthly basis which exceeds the quarterly cadence to maintain a strong influence on decision making.
 
      (Figure 19.)
Agile Sprint
The consultancy operates on a consistent two-week sprint as per the SCRUM guide. Each day follows a clear schedule to offer a regular checkpoint for the culmination of work. See Figure 9. In Appendix.

Budget and Sales forecast
The budget displayed outlined the expectation of revenue, expenses and profit over the next three years based on the assumptions provided as a part of Figure 20. The company displays a healthy growth over the three years with income scaling significantly in the third year.

There are significant possibilities for additional scaling through hires in the third year for developers to ensure there is no bottleneck and the addition of even more hires for the sales team.


 
 
