Investment needs
Due to expected initial losses within the first year due to early hiring to accelerate long term growth a personal retainer of £20,000 is available to the company for the purposes of covering hiring costs. Hiring costs are expected to exceed 50% of revenue until the third year from hence force it reaches an acceptable Salary Efficiency Ratio (Keelan E. 2024)

Other costs pertinent to the company have been deemed negligible or displaceable by other means. Hosting is to be completed on AWS though should the solution pose to be too financial disadvantages the procurement of a server within a home premise with redundancy in a back-up location are available for a negligible cost.

Personal capital for initial investment is at £20,000. Additionally, loans and financials due to unexpected overheads have lead times. It remains prudent to minimise cost when and where available. Additional investment is required to cover the expected peak negative deficit of £42000GBP in Q4 with additional to cover for unexpected costs that may arise. With the expected profits carrying over from Q1 & Q2 the peak negative deficit is to be bridged with an external loan of £10,000.

Blockers
The following are the expected blockers for the project:
-	Company sales pipeline. For time prior to sales agent hires there is a requirement for warm sales in order to generate quick wins.
-	Company sales agent quality and Sales volume. The expectation for sales agents is £80,000 in billing a year. This figure is based of recruitment experience within small companies of headcount under 15. There has been a notable lack of citable sources regarding this information available thus I have considered personal conversations from the owner of ‘Grean Peas’ a niche recruitment firm:  Where they have stated an expected return of x3-5 on Sales Salary for a company.
-	Code delivery time and testing processes. There is a strict timeline at the beginning of 6 months of development with a two-month lead before project launch.
-	The initial two months are required for DEMO product, with six months sufficient for a working client release. Early clients sign on will lead to the requirement of faster work output to exceed the six-month timeline.
-	Hiring timeframes leading to slower project sales & delivery

Long term business objectives

The implementation of Chatbots is currently a basic product line that does not offer the complexity and diversity that would ensure the long-term growth of the company. The company requires the ability to move into more mature and stable markets such as B-corps or enterprises to facilitate revenue growth into a touchpoint of seven figures. 

Other service offerings such as integration of services with customer applications are to be prioritised due to the greater potential upside. This will increase differentiation from competitors which usually only integrate with a select few applications.

Managing interactions, ensuring a good fit has been made and providing businesses with suitable change management to ease their transition toward Freon Chat. These actions are paramount for the future stages of the company’s development.

The fork towards voice agents for customer services for businesses and third parties is a future critical product line.
