Misc. Presentation details:

Justification for the initial two-month development lead-up? Timeline in general?
This has been left short enough to be able to display an MVP in time for promotion while allowing for enough development time for the eventual sign on which is to be expected by ~7 months. A later start of the product before signing on clients would cause too long before income is generated - jeopardising the companies financially.

Problem 
Currently small companies generally cannot provide comprehensive support services for their customers or properly leverage solutions that would take advantage of AI systems. The implementation of such solutions is often cost prohibitive or time consuming. Other concerns for small consultancies are scheduling…

Solution
Chatbots and Generative AI. The company offers a solution for implementation and off the shelf solutions to allow for easy access for a more diverse range of customers.
-	The skillset of project management, business development, sales and software development are not often found in a single individual thus the ability to be able to implement such a solution would be significantly more cost prohibitive for one.
-	Chatbots and Generative AI. The company offers an implementation service and off the shelf solutions.  This ensures access for a more diverse range of customers.
-	While the initial chat-bot itself is not a complex challenge, with there being a significant number of different resources available for its development. There are many nuances for developing a consistent and proper output. Certain issues such as the model not updating in real-time the time and date require additional development.
-	Then there are the complexities with integration with customer applications in a technical and business sense. Workflows have to be adjusted in order to better leverage the solution. Technical expertise gaps means that business run the risk of developing solutions with significant gaps in coverage and are prone to bugs.
-	Other issues for example are that the .css requires careful formatting to ensure a consistent design across all viewports. There is a significant time outlay for the production of a useful chatbot for companies for which it is just not an effective use of time. Internally-developed products do not carry an aesthetic quality found in FreonChat.
-	
Component level breakdown of product?

-	Pricing tiers: Purchase and subscription models
-	Front end: .css & Javascript
-	Chat model: OpenAI GPT-4o or GPT-3 dependant on price model. Other models available upon customer request. GPT-5 model is too expensive.
-	Hosting: AWS with local back-up potentially

Market

-> Small businesses primarily via subscription model, with custom packages available for more involved customers. 
-> Watford/London are priority for sales agent to ensure that the company can engage with customers on a personal basis and sustain a more complete end-to-end service model. Freon Chat aims to be an involved company as the common adage goes 80% of communication is non-verbal.
-> Mid/Long term to target SMEs -> Once the company has established a track record and made further product refinements the product push will be advanced to leverage greater company resource.
Financials

-	This figure is based on personal recruitment experience and the expectation from personal communications (Paolo Piscelli, 2025) that a sales agent will raise x3-5 their salary for a given company. This figure ties in well with Sales commission being around 20% for an exceptional consultant. I have provided a slightly lower expected sales value due to the new sector and the lack of associated commercial awareness. The value provided is £80,000.
-	With four sales Agent hires over three years. The expected profits per year are: £ (-)27,800, £95,700 and £396,250 respectively.
-	The financials account for steady hiring bringing the company to ~10 members of staff across the support, sales and development functions.`

